<description>&lt;p&gt;Iraqi security forces have intensified operations in the Kataib Hezbollah strongholds of Jurf al-Sakhar and Jurf al-Nasr, while Prime Minister Al-Zaidi ordered an inquiry into oil smuggling and threatened force to enforce a militia withdrawal deadline. Iran’s top IRGC commander arrived in Iraq for talks amid tensions with Kataib Hezbollah, and reports suggest Iran may be planning a dirty bomb attack in the US. Jordan and Iraq jointly blocked Telegram over national security and regulatory concerns, and the US consulate is conducting security tests in Erbil. Baghdad and Iran reached a deal for Kataib Hezbollah to leave Jurf al-Sakhar, and a former hostage said she was held in a militia stronghold targeted by the prime minister. The UCDP recorded 396 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE1iNmVhWG9MeTNkbFhMNGtWU3ZKbWxXbFhrRXlrUGhHcE5YZXE0YlFyNWo4ZmMxVVFzcDFmT09HWEZPUklJbC1ZN0JGTmMtNlE3S1liTkdlYVRXZ1RMd0ZHVWNkY1MzUG8xQ1dSS2F0alVRVjRib0Qw?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxPRWtoYndRVXNMdWx4LWVhMDgteGI1M2NYRDRFUFpkTkJvYzgxRVVSNzlNWDJvYk9xZEJQeXVlM2dEZ2hDelBkUzNaS24xejdJSnFVd2JJRjZZTGhTazdtM19jcHRpVGNxenl5N2JTLWU4YXFXYVlKRzJZeVQzZUthc29KOFRpMHFSallxT204Wk9xOVZmUTBtVDdoTU9uNmtFVEhhdkdPQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Amwaj.media&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPTFpYeW55N1Jmb0pmdmhzenRBaWRLODI3N0RlSjItS2ctUmd3al9JaDRIdTNyeWhuUGVpTXBrLXNpSDROSWVoTER